<article class="env-lemma" id="0CUI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CUI">Lemma <span data-tag="0CUI">70.4.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $(X_ i, f_{i'i})$ be an inverse systems over $I$ of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $X_ i$ is reduced for all $i$, then $X$ is reduced. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Observe that $\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits X_ i$ exists by Lemma <a href="/tag/07SF" data-tag="07SF">70.4.1</a>. Pick $0 \in I$ and choose an affine scheme $V_0$ and an étale morphism $U_0 \to X_0$. Then the affine schemes $U_ i = X_ i \times _{X_0} U_0$ are reduced. Hence $U = X \times _{X_0} U_0$ is a reduced affine scheme as a limit of reduced affine schemes: a filtered colimit of reduced rings is reduced. Since the étale morphisms $U \to X$ form an étale covering of $X$ as we vary our choice of $U_0 \to X_0$ we see that the lemma is true. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>